/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Brain tumor segmentation from Magnetic Resonance Imaging \(MRI\) is a critical step in clinical diagnosis, surgical planning, and post-operative monitoring. Traditional deep learning approaches rely entirely on visual feature extraction. However, in clinical practice, radiologists evaluate MRI scans in conjunction with prior knowledge, physiological hypotheses, and written clinical descriptions \(e.g., "ring-enhancing lesion with surrounding edema in the left temporal lobe"\).)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [10]
>>
